    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20051120.0032\n\nWELLINGTON, Nov. 20 , 2005 (Xinhua)\n\nNZ's greenhouse gas emissions increase\n\n\n\n\nNew Zealand is among the countries bucking an international trend of declining greenhouse gas levels.\n\nLocal media said Sunday that a report from the United Nations Climate Centre shows New Zealand's emissions have increased 22.5 percent since 1990.\n\nWorldwide there has been a 5.9 percent drop over the same period.\n\nNew Zealand has the eighth highest percentage greenhouse gas increase among the nations listed in the report.\n\nNearly half its emissions come from the agriculture sector.\n\nHowever there has been a huge increase in the level of discharges from transport since 1990.\n\nThe figures appear in a report from the United Nations body, ahead of the international climate change conference in Montreal later this month.\n\nNew Zealand is among the worst offenders, behind Spain, Monaco, Portugal, Greece, Ireland, Canada and Australia, said the report.",
